# TypeScript SDK and Berry bindings

`frontend/src/cos-sdk/` and the native modules in `components/berry_lang/src/` are one script API. A change to either side updates the other in the same change.

| Script global | Declarations | Native registration |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `log`, `action` | `index.d.ts` | `berry_runtime.cpp` |
| `console` | `console.d.ts` | `berry_runtime.cpp` |
| `fs` | `filesystem.d.ts` | `berry_runtime.cpp` |
| `net` | `network.d.ts` | `berry_runtime.cpp` |
| `ui` | `ui.d.ts` | `berry_ui.cpp` |

When adding or changing a script-facing function:

- Use the same Berry name, argument order, and return value on both sides. Names stay `snake_case`.
- Document the declaration with a TSDoc comment so the editor can show it on hover.
- Declare only functions the device can run, and register only functions the SDK exposes.
- When scripts can call it, add and compile a device example as described in the device script examples rule.

`language.d.ts` is the TypeScript subset the Berry compiler accepts. Keep it aligned with `frontend/src/ide/berry/`. It is not a native module.

```typescript
/** Integer scale of the 6x8 cell. `1` is 6x8 pixels. */
function set_font_size(size: 1 | 2 | 3): true | string;
```

That declaration matches `native_console_set_font_size`, registered as `console.set_font_size`.
